# DocAtlas documentation rules

When editing files matched by this rule:

## Structure

- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` — system design, components, data flow
- `docs/ONBOARDING.md` — setup and first-day guide
- `docs/RUNBOOK.md` — run, deploy, troubleshoot
- `docs/GLOSSARY.md` — terms and abbreviations

## Writing style

- Short sentences, clear headings, tables for reference data
- Commands in fenced code blocks — must be runnable as shown
- Link between docs instead of duplicating content

## Confidence tags

Place at section level:

- `[verified]` — confirmed recently against code or by running steps
- `[likely]` — based on code reading, not yet tested
- `[uncertain]` — needs owner follow-up; name owner or link issue
- `[planned]` — future behavior not yet shipped

## Checklist before finishing

- [ ] No bare `TODO` or `__JOURNEY_NAME__` left without explanation
- [ ] Commands tested or marked `[uncertain]`
- [ ] Glossary updated for new terms
- [ ] `docatlas drift` would pass

